# Test: plain OpenSSH receives clean exec output with zero answer frame lines,
# while an opt-in OpenSSH client sending ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 receives the exact
# record answer frame on stderr.
#
# One question: on the real SSH exec channel driven by OpenSSH against a live
# daemon, does a plain `ssh` session get clean rendered stdout (including pure
# JSON) with zero frame lines on stderr, while `ssh -o SendEnv=ZE_ANSWER_FRAME`
# with ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 receives matching stdout and the grammar-exact
# top/end/nay frame on stderr?
# Why a unit test cannot decide it: unit tests drive an in-process Go SSH client
# against an answerServer stub; only OpenSSH against a running `ze` daemon
# proves RFC 4254 Section 6.4 SendEnv propagation and real command dispatch
# across document, JSON, streamed, unknown-command, and failed-command paths.
#
# Flow:
# 1. Daemon starts with SSH and one configured BGP peer.
# 2. The native driver generates an ed25519 key pair and puts the public half
#    in the daemon's user, so OpenSSH authenticates with no password prompt.
# 3. Five commands run twice over `ssh`:
#    (a) Plain OpenSSH (no ZE_ANSWER_FRAME, -F /dev/null): asserts rendered
#        stdout (valid JSON for `show version | json`, >256 JSON rows for
#        `system command list | ndjson`, empty stdout on error) and ZERO
#        top/end/wrn/nay frame lines on stderr (empty stderr on success; plain
#        operator error line only on failure).
#    (b) Opt-in OpenSSH (-F /dev/null -o SendEnv=ZE_ANSWER_FRAME with
#        ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1): asserts stdout matches the plain run and stderr
#        carries the exact grammar-valid answer frame, verified by the compiled
#        frame checker (fixture06FrameCheck).
#
# The driver is OpenSSH and not `ze cli`, and that is the whole point of this
# test. `ze cli` is Ze's own client (ExecCommandStream, internal/component/cli/
# sshclient/answer.go); it always opts in via ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 and consumes the
# frame. Plain `ssh` consumes nothing and declares nothing, so its stderr must
# stay clean of protocol frames (AC-25 / declared-format-contradicts-payload
# 2026-10-10); when OpenSSH explicitly opts in via SendEnv=ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1,
# its raw stderr exposes the daemon's frame bytes unread and unrewritten.
#
# WHAT THE EXEC CHANNEL WRITES, and why `row` and `bad` are not here. The daemon
# RENDERS on this channel, because the format an operator sees comes from
# ze.cli.format and four of the six renderings run to several lines
# (writeExecAnswer, internal/component/ssh/answer.go). So the records reach the
# operator on stdout as rendered text, and stderr carries plain warnings/errors
# plus (when ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 is set) the frame around them: a head, a
# terminator, and a not-understood line for a command text that named no
# command. The record kinds belong to the multiplexed plugin connection, where
# answer-unconditional.ci asserts them. A `row` or a `bad` on THIS channel would
# be a rendering leaking into the frame, which is why the compiled checker
# refuses one.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-25 (plan/journal/declared-format-contradicts-payload.md,
# 2026-10-10) -- plain `ssh` without ZE_ANSWER_FRAME receives clean output
# (including valid JSON alone) and zero answer frame lines on stderr; opting in
# via ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 receives the head and terminator frame on stderr.
# VALIDATES: AC-4 -- the kind token starts at offset zero. The exec channel
# carries one answer, so no `#<id>` sits in front of it.
# VALIDATES: AC-13 -- no line carries a key=value pair. Every field is a
# three-byte word closed by a space, a counted number, or a counted text, and
# the compiled checker reaches each one by arithmetic with no scan anywhere.
# VALIDATES: AC-15 -- the head states no status: `top`, the item type, the
# envelope key, the column names, and nothing else.
# VALIDATES: AC-16 -- every token is a whole word: `top`, `end`, `nay` for the
# kinds this channel writes, `doc` and `map` for the item types it produces.
# VALIDATES: AC-17 -- an absent value is written `0:`, present and empty, so a
# line's field count never varies.
# VALIDATES: AC-20 -- a line ends at exactly one `\n`, and never at `\r\n`.
# PREVENTS: plugin frame trailers (`top doc 0: 0:`, `end 1 0 0:`) leaking onto
# stderr for plain `ssh <host> <command>` sessions, or opt-in framing breaking
# for clients that declare ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1.
# PREVENTS: a count of CHARACTERS reaching the wire where a count of BYTES
# belongs, which mis-slices every field after the first non-ASCII value.

# The compiled grammar reader owns the SHAPE of a line; the native driver owns
# the VALUES, so a change to either is read on its own terms.


# Process orchestration
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture plugin/exec-answer-unconditional:timeout=45s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: document -- a built payload is framed `top doc 0: 0:` and `end 1 0 0:`
expect=stderr:contains=OK: json -- plain SSH emitted clean JSON and opt-in framed `top doc 0: 0:` and `end 1 0 0:`
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: streamed -- a walk of [0-9]+ records is framed
expect=stderr:contains=OK: unknown -- a command text naming no command is the whole answer
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: failed -- a failed command states its message as 31 BYTES, not the 29 characters
expect=stderr:contains=OK: plain -- plain SSH received clean output with zero answer frame lines
expect=stderr:contains=OK: opt-in -- a client sending ZE_ANSWER_FRAME=1 read every frame by arithmetic
